  "articleBody": "Discovering a leak in your mobile home, whether it's from a pipe, roof, or window, is something you need to address immediately. Delaying repairs can lead to much bigger problems like extensive water damage, mold growth, and structural issues that compromise safety and habitability. Your first step should always be to stop the water source if possible—this might mean turning off the main water supply to the home. Next, thoroughly document the damage with photos and videos, noting the location and extent of the leak. This documentation is essential for any insurance claims or if you need to discuss the issue with a tenant. Then, assess the safety implications; is there any electrical wiring near the water? If so, be extremely careful and consider turning off the power to that area. Identify the source of the leak, as a small stain could indicate a much larger issue behind the wall or ceiling. Get professional estimates promptly. While you might be able to handle a minor drip, any significant leak, especially those affecting subfloors, electrical, or structural components, absolutely warrants a professional plumber or mobile home repair specialist to prevent recurring issues and ensure a lasting fix. Don't wait—get it fixed right away!",
